EXT. HOT AIR BALLOON BASKET - 3,000 FEET - DAY

Five bodies in a wicker basket built for three. Clouds below. One propane tank. Zero grace.

BARNABY CROOKE
We're fine, we're fine, it's just wind.

LUCINDA FAIRWEATHER
It's not wind, Barnaby, it's your weight!

DEZ
Who packed the sandwiches?

HALVORSEN
(over Dez)
We're descending. We are definitely descending.

BARNABY CROOKE
We are not descending, we are...

LUCINDA FAIRWEATHER
Hover! The word is hover!

PRIYA
Nobody touches the burner! I mean it!

DEZ
I just asked about sandwiches!

HALVORSEN
Priya, the altimeter is spinning.

PRIYA
It's supposed to spin!

BARNABY CROOKE
It is not supposed to spin!

LUCINDA FAIRWEATHER
Oh my God, there's a cow. There's a cow, and it's getting bigger.

DEZ
That's not a cow, that's a barn.

HALVORSEN
Everybody lean left!

PRIYA
Left is the other left!

BARNABY CROOKE
I proposed to you at 3,000 feet, Lucinda, and you said yes!

LUCINDA FAIRWEATHER
I said yes to a picnic!
